w: 1.~Re- joice, my heart, be glad and sing, A cheer- ful trust main- tain; 
w: 2.~He is thy Trea- sure, He thy Joy, Thy Life and Light and Lord, 
w: 3.~Why spend the day in blank des- pair, In rest- less thought the night? 
w: 4.~Did not His love and truth and pow'r Watch o'er thy child- hood day? 
w: 5.~His wis- dom nev- er plans in vain, Ne'er fal- ters or mis- takes; 
w: 6.~Up- on thy lips, then, lay thy hand And trust His guid- ing love;
w: 7.~O Lord I sing with lips and heart, Joy of my soul, to Thee:
w: 8.~Thou art the Fount of grace, I know, And Spring so full and free,
w: 9.~For what have all that live and move Through this wide world be- low
w: 10.~Who built the lof- ty fir- ma- ment? Who spread th'ex- panse of blue?
w: 11.~Who war- meth us in cold and frost? Who shields us from the wind?
w: 12.~Who is it life and health be- stows? Who keeps us with His hand
w: 13.~O Lord of this and all our store Thou art the au- thor blest;
w: 14.~Thou fee- dest us from year to year, And con- stant dost a- bide;
w: 15.~He ev- er will with pa- tience chide, His rod falls gent- ly down,
w: 16.~When si- lent woe thy bo- som rends, His pi- ty sees thy grief,
w: 17.~He knows how oft a Christ- ian weeps And why his tears now fall;
w: 18.~Our deep- est needs dost Thou sup- ply, Thou giv'st what lasts for aye.
